   "replace": "    /* The header is one flex row: brand, nav, then the workspace controls. The\n       nav had no min-width, so a flex item cannot shrink below its content —\n       once the tabs outgrew the window the nav pushed Tools and the right-hand\n       controls clean off the edge instead of scrolling. At 1440px that already\n       cost Property Info and the whole Tools menu. Let the nav shrink and\n       scroll; pin everything either side of it. */\n    nav{min-width:0;overflow-x:auto;overflow-y:hidden;scrollbar-width:none;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch}\n    nav::-webkit-scrollbar{display:none}\n    .nav-dd{flex:0 0 auto}\n    /* Phone: same row, tighter, and the dropdown opens the other way so it does\n       not hang off the right edge. */\n    @media (max-width:760px){\n      body{font-size:13px}\n      .nav-btn{padding:11px 11px 9px;font-size:12px}\n      .nav-dd-menu{right:auto;left:0}\n      .spl-box{width:auto;max-width:94vw}\n      /* 390px of header cannot hold the brand, the tabs, Tools AND the three\n         workspace controls. The controls are the ones you touch least - the\n         profile is a per-browser declutter setting, Clear data is a once-ever\n         action, the property count is a stat - so they stand down on a phone\n         and the tab strip gets the room. */\n      #nav-profile,#btn-clear-all,#hdr-props{display:none!important}\n    }\n    /* Print */\n    @media print{",
